INSERT INTO `books` VALUES (11,'C++ Primer','Barbara E. Moo, JosÃ©e Lajoie, Stanley B. Lippman',NULL,2012,'This book teaches C++ programming, from basic language features to more advanced concepts such as classes, templates, and the Standard Library. It provides explanations and examples that help readers develop a strong foundation in writing reliable C++ programs.','','Addison-Wesley Professional',3,'Available','2026-10-16 04:37:23'),(12,'The Gene: An Intimate History','Siddhartha Mukherjee',NULL,2016,'This book explores the history of genetics and the scientific discoveries that helped researchers understand heredity and genes. It connects scientific developments with human stories and discusses the possibilities and ethical questions surrounding genetic research.','','Scribner',3,'Available','2026-10-16 04:49:41'),(13,'Grokking Algorithms','Aditya Y. Bhargava',NULL,2016,'This book introduces important computer science algorithms using simple explanations, illustrations, and practical examples. Topics include binary search, sorting, recursion, hash tables, graphs, and greedy algorithms, making it suitable for beginners learning problem-solving techniques.','','Manning Publications',3,'Available','2026-10-16 04:51:22'),(14,'Learning SQL','Alan Beaulieu',NULL,2020,'This book explains how to use SQL to retrieve, organize, and manipulate data stored in relational databases. It covers queries, joins, subqueries, data modification, and other useful database operations that help readers work with real-world data.','','O\'Reilly Media, Inc.',3,'Available','2026-10-16 04:52:14'),(15,'Database System Concepts','Avi Silberschatz, Henry F. Korth, S. Sudarshan',NULL,2019,'This textbook explains the fundamental concepts behind database management systems, including relational databases, SQL, database design, transactions, and storage. It also introduces topics such as indexing, concurrency control, and database recovery, which are important for understanding how database systems work internally.','','McGraw-Hill',3,'Available','2026-10-16 04:55:46'),(16,'The Insects: An Outline of Entomology','P. J. Gullan, P. S. Cranston',NULL,2014,'This textbook provides a detailed introduction to insects, including their anatomy, physiology, behavior, classification, and evolution. It also explores their ecological roles, relationships with other organisms, and importance in agriculture, medicine, and environmental science.','','Wiley-Blackwell',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:44:08'),(17,'Six Easy Pieces','Richard P. Feynman',NULL,1994,'This book presents selected introductory physics lectures by Richard Feynman in an accessible format. It introduces fundamental ideas such as atoms, energy, motion, and the relationship between physical laws, helping readers understand the basic principles of the natural world.','','Addison-Wesley',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:45:46'),(18,'Chemistry: The Central Science','Theodore L. Brown, H. Eugene LeMay Jr., Bruce E. Bursten, and coauthors',NULL,2023,'This textbook introduces the main principles of chemistry, including atomic structure, chemical bonding, reactions, gases, thermodynamics, and chemical equilibrium. It uses worked examples and practical applications to explain how chemical concepts relate to everyday life and other scientific fields.','','Pearson',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:47:41'),(19,'The Personal MBA','Josh Kaufman',NULL,2010,'This book introduces essential business concepts without requiring readers to complete a formal business degree. It discusses marketing, sales, finance, operations, productivity, and decision-making to help readers understand how businesses operate and create value.','','Portfolio (Penguin Group)',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:51:39'),(20,'Entrepreneurship: Successfully Launching New Ventures','Bruce R. Barringer, R. Duane Ireland',NULL,2024,'This textbook guides readers through the process of developing a business idea and turning it into a functioning enterprise. It covers opportunity recognition, feasibility analysis, business plans, financing, marketing, and strategies for growing a new business.','','Pearson',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:53:07'),(21,'Financial Accounting','Robert Libby, Patricia A. Libby, Frank Hodge',NULL,2023,'This textbook teaches the fundamentals of financial accounting and explains how businesses record and report financial information. It covers financial statements, accounting transactions, revenue, expenses, assets, liabilities, and the use of accounting information in business decisions.','','McGraw Hill',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:53:51'),(22,'Accounting Made Simple','Mike Piper',NULL,2013,'This book introduces accounting concepts in straightforward language for readers without an accounting background. It explains the accounting equation, debits and credits, financial statements, and basic financial ratios to help readers understand a company\'s financial position.','','Simple Subjects',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:55:05'),(23,'1984','George Orwell',NULL,1949,'Set in a dystopian society ruled by an authoritarian government, the novel follows Winston Smith as he struggles against constant surveillance and strict control over information and thought. The story explores themes of propaganda, censorship, freedom, and the dangers of unchecked political power.','','Seker and Warburg',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:56:44'),(24,'Dune','Frank Herbert',NULL,1965,'The novel follows Paul Atreides, a young nobleman whose family becomes involved in a dangerous struggle for control of the desert planet Arrakis. Through its themes of politics, religion, ecology, and survival, the story explores how power and natural resources can shape civilizations.','','Chilton Books',3,'Available','2026-10-16 07:57:25'),(25,'The Pragmatic Programmer','David Thomas, Andrew Hunt',NULL,2019,'This book teaches practical approaches to software development, including writing maintainable code, debugging, testing, and managing complexity. It encourages programmers to take responsibility for their work and continuously improve their technical skills.','','Addison-Wesley Professional',3,'Available','2026-10-16 08:39:50'),(26,'Clean Code: A Handbook of Agile Software Craftsmanship','Robert C. Martin',NULL,2008,'This book explains how to write readable, organized, and maintainable source code. Through examples and programming principles, it shows how meaningful names, small functions, and thoughtful design can make software easier to understand and modify.','','Prentice Hall',3,'Available','2026-10-16 08:41:12'),(27,'The Art of Computer Programming, Volume 1: Fundamental Algorithms','Donald E. Knuth',NULL,1997,'his technical reference explores the mathematical foundations of computer programming, including algorithms, data structures, and basic computational methods. It is especially useful for readers who want a deeper understanding of algorithm design and analysis.','','Addison-Wesley',3,'Available','2026-10-16 08:42:32'),(28,'Sapiens: A Brief History of Humankind','Yuval Noah Harari',NULL,2015,'This book traces human history from early human species to modern societies. It examines how shared beliefs, agriculture, money, politics, and scientific developments have shaped human civilization.','','Harper',3,'Available','2026-10-16 08:46:42'),(29,'The Martian','Andy Weir',NULL,2014,'Astronaut Mark Watney becomes stranded on Mars after his crew believes he has died during an emergency evacuation. Using scientific knowledge, engineering, and creativity, he works to survive on the planet while attempting to contact Earth and find a way home.','','Crown Publishing Group',3,'Available','2026-10-16 08:48:20'),(30,'The Book Thief','Markus Zusak',NULL,2005,'Set in Nazi Germany during World War II, the novel follows Liesel Meminger, a young girl who discovers comfort and meaning through books. As she witnesses war and persecution, she learns about friendship, courage, loss, and the power of words.','','Picador',3,'Av